{status:"approved",title:"Updated Call Script",section:"Updated Script — Core Rules, Discovery and Lead Routing",tags:["secondary script","updated script","call script","discovery","lead stages"],content:"INDIFRAME WINDOWS & DOORS — SECONDARY / UPDATED SCRIPT (English source retained).\nCORE CALL RULES: Treat every call like a helpful consultation, not a rigid questionnaire. Ask one question at a time and allow the customer to respond. Listen actively, acknowledge concerns and keep the tone supportive. Keep explanations simple and avoid unnecessary technical terminology. Do not criticise competitors or local fabricators; redirect discussion toward IndiFrame's value. Do not promise unauthorised discounts, exact delivery dates, structural approvals, wind-load calculations, mm-level specifications, chamber counts or technical details requiring validation. Every connected call must end with a clear agreed next action. Reconfirm customer requirement, agreed action, responsible team, date and time wherever applicable. Installation is best planned after granite or marble sill work is completed.\nSIX DISCOVERY QUESTIONS: 1. Project Type — “Is this project for your personal residential home or commercial property?” 2. Site Location — “Which specific city and area/locality is your construction site located in?” 3. Stakeholder Role — “Are you managing the build directly, or working with an architect or interior designer?” 4. Construction Stage — “What stage is the site currently in — Foundation, Brickwork, Plastering, or Finishing?” 5. Quantity Estimate — “Approximately how many window and door apertures/openings do you need to cover?” 6. Aperture Readiness — “Have internal and external plastering been completed around all window openings?”\nLEAD STAGES: C0 New Unqualified Lead — initial lead ingestion; initiate first call immediately upon assignment. C1 Future Potential Lead — foundation, slab, brickwork, structural, granite work or plastering incomplete; schedule follow-up based on projected readiness date. C2 Active/Qualified Lead — plastering complete and apertures ready; post customer details in Daily Leads WhatsApp Group, tag designated Regional Sales Owner, and offer free site consultation or Experience Centre visit. C7 Routed to Partner (B2F) — outside direct coverage; offer authorised Green Fortune partner route and update CRM. C4 Won — payment done/manufacturing started; update CRM and initiate order processing/manufacturing handover. C6 Lost — record specific reason, update CRM and schedule nurturing/feedback where applicable.\nPRICING & WARRANTY AS STATED IN THIS SECONDARY DOCUMENT: Starting price from ₹450 per sq. ft. onwards plus applicable GST; do not calculate custom prices during initial qualification. The document states 15-year profile warranty, 5-year hardware warranty and 7-year colour warranty. For current operational answers, follow the separately approved Final Script and Brand & Product SOP where they supersede this secondary document.\nPROTECTED ACCOUNTS: Outbound qualification or dialling on accounts owned by Nikunj Mehta, Nayan Panchal, Sushant Gosh or Ravi Boliipogu is strictly prohibited; these are high-value corporate/project accounts managed at management level.\nLEAD CONTROL: C1 future lead follow-up is based on projected readiness. C2 qualified lead handover goes to Daily Leads WhatsApp Group and Regional Sales Owner. C7 unserviceable lead is routed to authorised Green Fortune partner and logged as C7 / ROUTE TO B2F. This uploaded document also contains a conflicting older retry line of maximum 9 attempts across 12 days; current authoritative cadence remains the Final Script's 15 attempts across 9 calendar days."},
{status:"approved",title:"Updated Call Script",section:"Updated Script — Customer Education and Renovation",tags:["secondary script","renovation","uPVC explanation","brand introduction","blank call","abusive language"],content:"BRAND INTRODUCTION IF CUSTOMER IS NOT FAMILIAR: “Sir/Ma'am, just to give you a quick idea about Indi Frame, we provide different types of windows and doors based on customer requirements, design preferences, and project needs. Our team can also guide you on which solution/type would be most suitable for your project.”\nWHAT IS uPVC: “uPVC stands for Unplasticized Polyvinyl Chloride. It is a strong, durable, and low-maintenance material commonly used for manufacturing windows and doors. It can provide good insulation and may help reduce outside noise and heat, depending on the overall window or door configuration.”\nQUICK EXPLANATION: IndiFrame provides uPVC and aluminium windows and doors in sliding, casement, fixed, tilt & turn, and slide & fold configurations. The team understands the customer's requirement and guides them on suitable options.\nMANDATORY RENOVATION SEQUENCE: Confirm whether customer/their team will remove existing windows and doors before IndiFrame work starts. Explain clearly that the customer/their team must remove them; IndiFrame does not provide uninstalling. Confirm acceptance. If agreed, collect expected removal/site-readiness date and convenient follow-up date/time. Do not confirm installation before existing windows and doors are removed. If customer cannot arrange removal, explain the work can start only after removal; invite them to reconnect when site is ready. The uploaded script contains the website contact number 9959083498.\nABUSIVE / INAPPROPRIATE LANGUAGE: First and second attempt: “I would request you to kindly use professional language.” If there is no positive response: “As there is no positive response from your side, your call is being disconnected. Thank you for considering IndiFrame. We look forward to assisting you whenever you are ready. Have a wonderful day ahead.”\nBLANK CALL / NO RESPONSE: First attempt: “Good morning, this is [Agent Name], calling from IndiFrame Windows and Doors.” Second attempt: “Good morning, this is [Agent Name], calling from IndiFrame Windows and Doors, please respond if you are on the call.” Closing: “As there is no response, the call is being disconnected. Thank you for considering IndiFrame. We look forward to assisting you whenever you are ready. Have a wonderful day ahead.”\nEXTENDED HOLD: The source script includes first/second-attempt lines for a customer putting the call on hold, followed by a polite disconnection close when there is no response.\nVOICEMAIL: “Hello, this is [Agent Name] calling from IndiFrame Windows and Doors regarding your enquiry. Please call us back at your convenience. Thank you.”"},
{status:"approved",title:"Updated Call Script",section:"Updated Script — Scenario A: Digital Ad Lead",tags:["secondary script","digital lead","Meta","Facebook","Instagram","website","WhatsApp"],content:"CONTEXT: Fresh enquiries from Meta, Google, Website, WhatsApp or another digital channel.\nA1 OPENING & PERMISSION: “Good evening, Sir, I am calling from IndiFrame, a premium brand in high-quality uPVC and Aluminum products/windows and doors. We received your enquiry regarding Windows & Doors on [Facebook/Instagram/WhatsApp/Website]. Is this a good time for a quick conversation?”\nA2 CORE REQUIREMENT & PROJECT TYPE: Ask whether they need windows or doors; new construction or renovation; residential or commercial; and the specific city and area/locality.\nA3 QUANTITY, MATERIAL & STYLE: “How many windows and doors do you need? A rough count is completely fine for now.” Ask whether they have a style in mind: sliding, casement, fixed, tilt & turn, or slide & fold.\nA4 CONSTRUCTION STAGE, READINESS & TIMELINE: Ask current stage (foundation, brickwork, plastering or finishing), approximate installation/finalisation timeline, and whether granite or marble sill work is complete. If customer wants installation before granite/marble work, note it and say Sales will check site condition and confirm suitable installation stage.\nA5 STAKEHOLDER: Ask whether customer makes the final purchase decision or an architect, builder, contractor, designer or family member is also involved. If others are involved, invite them to the consultation.\nA6 CUSTOMER QUESTIONS / VOC: If asked why choose IndiFrame, explain pan-India brand headquartered in Hyderabad, uPVC and aluminium windows/doors, professional measurement, trained installation and dedicated after-sales support. Do not add unapproved technical benefits for uPVC. For high price or competitor comparison, acknowledge concern and say Sales will explain pricing based on product, size, configuration, hardware and project requirement. Do not promise discount, compare unsupported prices or give unsupported final quotation. For installation or after-sales questions, explain that teams coordinate based on site condition and route to relevant team. For location, explain service coverage and nearest Experience Centre guidance. Factory visit can be coordinated. Do not promise exact installation timeline.\nA7 CLOSING: Reconfirm quantity/type, residential/commercial project and location. Ask customer preference for Sales Team discussion, site consultation, Experience Centre visit or callback. If proceeding, confirm next action and date/time. If later, confirm callback date/time. If not interested, politely ask reason only if comfortable, note feedback and close: “Thank you for considering IndiFrame. We look forward to assisting you whenever you are ready. Have a wonderful day ahead.”"},
{status:"approved",title:"Updated Call Script",section:"Updated Script — Scenarios B and C: Field and Expo Leads",tags:["secondary script","field spotted lead","expo lead","event lead"],content:"SCENARIO B — FIELD SPOTTED LEAD. Context: Lead collected through field sales, active construction site, site visit or walk-by interaction.\nB1 OPENING: “Good morning. I am calling on behalf of IndiFrame Windows and Doors, a premium brand specializing in high-quality uPVC and Aluminum products/windows and doors. Am I speaking with Mr./Ms. [Customer Name]? Our field officer [Name] recently noted your construction work at [Location]. Since your site is under construction, is this a good time to ask a few questions to understand your requirements and guide you properly?”\nB2 REQUIREMENT: If spotter details are unavailable, ask whether windows, doors or both are required, rough quantity and type, material preference if known, and styles such as sliding, casement, fixed, tilt & turn or slide & fold. If details exist, read them back and confirm quantity/type and project location.\nB3 SITE STAGE: If unavailable, ask construction stage, expected installation stage, and whether granite/marble sill work is complete. Confirm the stakeholder details if provided in this secondary script. Recap recorded information and ask if correct.\nEND-TO-END NEXT STEP: Offer Sales Team callback, site consultation, Experience Centre visit, factory visit or partner follow-up as appropriate.\nB4 SITE CONSULTATION CLOSE: Reconfirm requirement and location; explain free site consultation, professional measurements, custom manufacturing, trained installation and after-sales support; collect a convenient date/time for Sales to coordinate consultation; confirm follow-up and close politely.\nB5 SALES CALLBACK: If customer wants immediate callback, reconfirm requirement and concern; the secondary script states that Sales may call within the next one hour. If callback is later, capture date/time, reconfirm requirement and concern, and confirm the team will connect then.\nSCENARIO C — EXPO / EVENT LEAD. Context: Customer visited IndiFrame display, exhibition or public event.\nC1 OPENING: Identify the customer, event name/date/location and ask if it is a good time. Explain the call is to understand window/door requirement.\nC2 REQUIREMENT: Confirm whether windows, doors or both; quantity/type from event notes; project location; uPVC/aluminium preference or need for technical guidance; style preference; and main priority such as appearance, ventilation, natural light, sound reduction, ease of operation, safety, heat reduction or privacy.\nC3 PROJECT STAGE: Ask new construction/upcoming renovation, current stage, plastering readiness, expected installation stage, granite/marble sill completion and stakeholder involvement.\nC4 SITE CONSULTATION: Reconfirm requirement and location, explain consultation and measurement support, collect convenient date/time and confirm Sales follow-up.\nC5 SALES CALLBACK: Confirm immediate or scheduled callback, requirement, concern and timing; explain the next step and close.\nC6 EXPERIENCE CENTRE VISIT: Confirm requirement/location, selected Experience Centre, preferred visit date/time, and coordination by team.\nC7 FACTORY VISIT: Confirm requirement/location and Medchal factory preference, collect factory visit date/time and confirm team coordination."},
{status:"approved",title:"Updated Call Script",section:"Updated Script — Scenarios D and E: Follow-up and Partner Leads",tags:["secondary script","warm lead","stage follow-up","construction delay","partner lead","C7"],content:"SCENARIO D — STAGE FOLLOW-UP / WARM LEAD / CONSTRUCTION DELAY. Context: Existing lead waiting on construction progress, budget, timing or decision.\nOPENING & PERMISSION: Identify self and IndiFrame, refer to previous conversation [number of days/weeks] about windows/doors for [Project/Location], ask if it is a good time, and ask for construction/renovation updates.\nD2 RECONFIRM REQUIREMENT: Recap previous quantity and type; ask if requirement/quantity changed and whether quotation/details have been reviewed or there is a concern.\nD3 CONSTRUCTION DELAY: Acknowledge that timelines change. Explain installation is best planned after granite/marble sill work; ask current wall/sill stage and expected readiness.\nD4 BUDGET / PRICE: Acknowledge budget management; ask whether customer is comparing a branded provider or local vendor; explain IndiFrame value through consultation, measurements, custom manufacturing, trained installation and after-sales support. Do not make unsupported comparisons.\nNEXT STEP: Offer Sales Team callback, site consultation, Experience Centre visit, factory visit or partner follow-up.\nD5 FUTURE FOLLOW-UP: Reconfirm quantity/type, project/location, concern and responsible team; confirm follow-up date/time.\nD6 IMMEDIATE SITE CONSULTATION: Reconfirm windows/doors and location; confirm Sales follow-up date/time to arrange consultation and next steps.\nSCENARIO E — LOCATION OUTSIDE DIRECT SERVICE AREA / GREEN FORTUNE FABRICATOR. Context: Project outside direct IndiFrame installation coverage and should be connected to authorised Green Fortune partner.\nE1 OPENING: Introduce IndiFrame and ask permission for a quick conversation.\nE2 REQUIREMENT: Confirm windows/doors/both, enquiry quantity/type and project location; understand material/style only if relevant. Explain that direct installation teams operate selectively in main service locations and that the team will connect the customer with the appropriate Green Fortune fabricator partner.\nE3 SITE STAGE: Ask new construction/renovation, stage, expected installation stage and granite/marble sill readiness. The uploaded secondary script also includes a stakeholder question.\nE4/E5 PARTNER CALLBACK: Reconfirm requirement, location and concern; explain concerned partner team can contact the customer; capture immediate or preferred scheduled callback and close politely. Log partner routing appropriately."},
{status:"approved",title:"Updated Call Script",section:"Updated Script — Customer Objections, Timeline and Follow-up",tags:["secondary script","objections","VOC","timeline","callback","quotation"],content:"CUSTOMER NOT FAMILIAR WITH INDIFRAME: Explain that IndiFrame is a pan-India brand headquartered in Hyderabad, providing uPVC and aluminium windows and doors. The secondary source lists service across Andhra Pradesh, Maharashtra and Telangana and describes Experience Centre locations at Kukatpally, Jubilee Hills (opening shortly in the source) and Malad West. Always use current directory status for location availability.\nOBJECTION RESPONSES: “Why should I choose IndiFrame?” — Explain organised end-to-end process: professional consultation, suitable product guidance, standardised manufacturing, trained installation, warranty and after-sales support. “Why choose over local fabricator?” — Acknowledge and describe process/value without criticising local providers. “What makes IndiFrame different?” — Clarity, project stage/readiness guidance and coordination with suitable team. “Will you help choose window/door type?” — Team understands requirement, location, opening size, usage, design preference and stage, then guides on options. “Can I visit products?” — Offer nearest available Experience Centre. “Will I get after-sales support?” — Explain applicable warranty and support route. “Why do you need location?” — To check service coverage, assign local team and coordinate support. “How did you get my number?” — Explain it was registered through enquiry source where customer expressed interest. “I’m exploring” — acknowledge and offer guidance when ready. “Send details” — confirm whether windows, doors or both. “I only want price” — the secondary script quotes starting ₹450/sq ft onwards plus applicable GST; follow current approved pricing rules before quoting. “I’m busy” — ask convenient callback time. “Remove my number” — acknowledge and update system as requested. “Local fabricators are cheaper” — discuss overall value, material quality, professional measurement, manufacturing, installation, warranty and after-sales. “Already purchased” — congratulate and invite future enquiries. “Project postponed” — note postponement and ask follow-up timing. “Chose another brand” — thank customer and ask reason only if comfortable.\nTIMELINE RESPONSES: Immediately — arrange relevant next step after site readiness/technical confirmation. Within 1 month — plan consultation around construction schedule. 1–3 months — plan consultation, design, measurement and next steps. 3–6 months — schedule follow-up closer to installation timeline. Price concern — acknowledge budget and offer Sales discussion on overall value and suitable options.\nSTAGE-WISE FOLLOW-UP: Recap previous requirement; site consultation pending — ask preferred date/time; consultation completed — ask whether details reviewed; quotation shared — ask if reviewed/clarification needed; price high/comparing competitors — discuss suitability, hardware, installation, warranty and service; needs time/family decision — ask suitable follow-up; project delayed — note pause and callback date; selected another brand — ask brand/reason if comfortable; ready to proceed/order pending — confirm order and next steps."},
{status:"approved",title:"Updated Call Script",section:"Updated Script — Visits, Golden Closing and CRM Checklist",tags:["secondary script","factory visit","experience centre","closing","qualification checklist","CRM"],content:"FACTORY / EXPERIENCE CENTRE MODULE: Offer Medchal factory, Experience Centre, site consultation or later callback. Explain that the Medchal factory visit can help customer understand manufacturing process. The secondary source lists Kukatpally, Jubilee Hills and Malad West Experience Centre locations; use current Experience Centre & Dealer Showroom Directory for latest address/status.\nGOLDEN CLOSING: “Thank you, [Customer Name]. That gives me a clear understanding of your requirements.” Reconfirm quantity/type of windows and doors and residential/commercial project location. Confirm next step — Sales Team callback / site consultation / Experience Centre visit / factory visit / partner follow-up — and relevant team, date and time. Ask “Have I understood that correctly?” Confirm and explain follow-up. Close with thanks and a polite day wish.\nMASTER QUALIFICATION CHECKLIST: Customer name; contact number; lead source; city; locality; project address/landmark; residential/commercial; new construction/renovation; construction stage; windows required/quantity; doors required/quantity; approximate quantity; uPVC/aluminium/not decided; product type/configuration; primary requirement; budget sensitivity; expected installation timeline; decision-maker/stakeholder details; architect/contractor/builder details; competitor status; site consultation requirement; Experience Centre interest; quotation status; customer objection; next action; next follow-up date/time; final lead disposition.\nMANDATORY CLOSING CHECK: Customer name; windows quantity/type; doors quantity/type; project location; agreed next action; relevant team; date; time; visit type if applicable; expected callback timeframe. Never end a connected call with vague “Okay, our team will contact you.” Confirm sequence: Requirement → Relevant Team → Action → Date → Time → Expected Follow-Up.\nCRM & OPERATIONAL HANDOVER: C2 qualified leads — post contact details in Daily Leads WhatsApp Group and tag Regional Sales Owner. C1 future leads — CRM follow-up based on projected construction/plastering readiness. C7 unserviceable leads — route to authorised Green Fortune partner and record C7 / ROUTE TO B2F. Unanswered calls — source's older retry section says max 9 attempts across 12 calendar days; current authoritative retry cadence is 15 attempts across 9 calendar days. Never outbound qualify or dial protected accounts. LOST / CLOSED REASONS in source: Not Interested; Wrong Number; Wrong Lead; Duplicate Lead; Already Purchased; Competitor Selected; Project Cancelled; Project Postponed; Budget Issue; Price Too High; Location Not Serviceable; No Requirement; Customer Unreachable."}
,
{status:"approved",title:"Updated Call Script",section:"Complete Updated Script (English)",tags:["updated script","secondary script","call script","scenario","objections","follow-up","closing"],content:"<PARSED TEXT FOR PAGE: 1 / 16>\n                            INDIFRAME WINDOWS & DOORS\n     Treat every call like a helpful consultation, not a rigid questionnaire.\n\n     Ask one question at a time and allow the customer to respond before continuing.\n\n     Listen actively, acknowledge concerns, and keep the tone supportive throughout the conversation.\n\n     Keep explanations simple and avoid unnecessary technical terminology.\n\n     Do not criticize competitors or local fabricators; redirect the discussion toward Indi Frame's value.\n\n     Do not promise unauthorized discounts, exact delivery dates, structural approvals, wind-load calculations,\n\n      mm-level specifications, chamber counts, or other technical details that require technical validation.\n\n     Every connected call must end with a clear, agreed next action.\n\n     Before ending, reconfirm the customer's requirement and the agreed action, team, date, and time wherever\n\n      applicable.\n\n     Installation is best planned after granite or marble sill work is completed, helping ensure proper fit and\n\n      reduce the risk of site damage.\n\n\n      2. Mandatory Discovery Questions\n\n      These six questions should be completed before assigning the lead stage, wherever the conversation allows.\n\n     Project Type: Is this project for your personal residential home or commercial property?\n\n     Site Location: Which specific city and area/locality is your construction site located in?\n\n     Stakeholder Role: Are you managing the build directly, or working with an architect or interior designer?\n\n     Construction Stage: What stage is the site currently in — Foundation, Brickwork, Plastering, or Finishing?\n\n     Quantity Estimate: Approximately how many window and door apertures/openings do you need to cover?\n\n     Aperture Readiness: Have internal and external plastering been completed around all window openings?\n\n\n      3. Lead Stage & Routing Rules\n\n     C0 – New Unqualified Lead: Initial lead ingestion. Initiate the first call immediately upon assignment.\n\n     C1 – Future Potential Lead: Foundation, slab, brickwork, or plastering is incomplete. Schedule follow-up\n\n      based on the projected readiness date.\n\n     C2 – Active / Qualified Lead: Plastering is complete and apertures are ready for audit. Post contact details in\n\n      the Daily Leads WhatsApp Group, tag the designated Regional Sales Owner, and offer a free site audit or\n\n      showroom/Experience Centre visit.\n\n     C7 – Routed to Partner (B2F): Site is outside direct IndiFrame service coverage. Offer the authorized Green\n\n      Fortune partner route and update CRM accordingly.\n\n     Pricing rule: quote only Starts from ₹450 per sq ft onwards plus applicable GST. Do not calculate custom\n\n      prices during initial qualifications.\n\n     Authorized warranty claims: 15-year profile warranty, 5-year hardware warranty, and 7-year color warranty.\n\n\nAcknowledged. Outbound qualification or dialing on protected accounts owned by Nikunj Mehta, Nayan Panchal,\nSushant Gosh, or\nRavi Boliipogu is strictly prohibited. These are high-value corporate/project accounts managed directly at the\nmanagement level\n\n\n\n\n                                The Six Mandatory Discovery Questions\n          Parameter                           Approved English Question                     Expected Output / Control\n\n\n                                Is this project for your personal residential home or     Residential / Commercial / Villa /\n         Project Type\n                                                 commercial property?                               Apartment\n\n                                    Which specific city and area/locality is your          Area name + PIN code; verify\n         Site Location\n                                           construction site located in?                          serviceability\n\n                                  Are you managing the build directly, or working        Self / Architect / Civil Contractor /\n       Stakeholder Role\n                                       with an architect or interior designer?                        Designer\n\n                                  What stage is the site currently in — Foundation,     Foundation / Brickwork / Plastering /\n      Construction Stage\n                                        Brickwork, Plastering, or Finishing?                          Interiors\n\n                                    Approximately how many window and door\n      Quantity Estimate                                                                   Estimated window & door count\n                                     apertures/openings do you need to cover?\n\n      Aperture Readiness             Have internal and external plastering been             Yes (Ready) / No (In Progress\n<PARSED TEXT FOR PAGE: 2 / 16>\n                                                 completed around all window openings?\n         1: FUTURE LEAD                                            2: ACTIVE LEAD                                                        3: UNSERVICEABLE\n\n Site Stage: Foundation / Slab /\n                                                                                                                          Site Location: Outside Direct Company\n Brickwork / Structural / Granite          Site Stage: Plastering Completed / Ready Openings\n                                                                                                                                                 Coverage\n              Work\n\n  Action: Mark Stage C1. Quote             Action: Mark Stage C2. Quote starting rate (₹450/sq                              Action: Offer Green Fortune Partner\n\n  starting rate (₹450/sq ft+GST).                    ft+). Pitch free site audit/ showroom                                                Fabricator option.\n\nFollow-up: Set callback schedule             Handover: Post to WhatsApp Group & Tagged                                       Routing: Transfer Laed to B2F / Log\n\n    (15 attempts over 9 days).                                 Regional Sales Owner.                                                       Stage C7 in CRM.\n\n                                                  STANDARD OPERATING PROTOCOL &\n\n   PARAMETER CATEGORY                                         OPERATIONAL RULES                                                     ENFORCEMENT DETAILS\n\n                                            Agents are strictly authorized to quote ONLY the                                     STRICT RED LINE No custom\n    Pricing Quotation Rules                 standard baseline starting rate: Starts from ₹450                            calculations, single-window estimates, or\n                                                                 per sq ft onwards.                                          unauthorized discounts permitted.\n                                           Never commit to exact delivery timelines, mm-level Defer technical specs to the technical site\nTechnical & Scope Boundaries                  specifications, chamber counts, or wind-load                               audit team during TAO (Transfer Away /\n                                                     calculations during initial discovery.                                            Technical Operations).\n                                             If the site location is beyond direct Indi-Frame\n   Unserviceable Locations                 installation boundaries, offer referral to authorized                             Log as C7 (ROUTE TO B2F) in CRM.\n                                                      Green Fortune partner fabricators.\n  Unreachable Leads & Retry               For unanswered calls, follow the mandatory retry of Execute a maximum of 9 call attempts\n          Cadence                                 cadence before archiving the lead.                across 12 calendar days.\n\n\n                                          CRM STAGE CLASSIFICATION & HANDOVER MATRIX\n\n\n\n   Stage            Description                             Qualification trigger                                       Required next action and routing\n\n\n    C0           New unqualified lead            Initial lead ingestion from marketing channels                      Make call attempt 1 immediately on assignment.\n\n                                                                                                         Schedule a CRM follow-up based on the projected plastering / readiness\n                                             Foundation, slab, brickwork, structural, granite work or    date. For uPVC enquiries, quote the starting rate of ₹450/sq ft onwards\n    C1           Future potential lead\n                                                             plastering incomplete                        plus GST. Route aluminium enquiries to Sales without providing prices,\n                                                                                                                               specifications or timelines.\n                                                                                                          Post the customer’s contact details in the Daily Leads WhatsApp group\n                                                                                                            and tag the designated Regional Sales Owner (Section 22). For uPVC\n                                                                                                           enquiries, quote the starting rate; route aluminium enquiries to Sales\n                                                                                                           without providing prices, specifications or timelines. Offer a free site\n                                                                                                                         consultation or an Experience Centre visit.\n    C2          Active / qualified lead             Plastering fully complete; openings ready\n                                                                                                        Update the lead status as 'Won' in the CRM, initiate the order processing /\n                                                                                                          manufacturing handover, and share the confirmation details with the\n                                                                                                                                        customer.\n                                                                                                        Record the specific reason for loss in the CRM, update lead status to 'Lost',\n                                                                                                         and schedule a long-term nurturing or feedback follow-up if applicable.\n                                                                                                         Offer the authorised Green Fortune partner route (Scenario E). Transfer\n    C7          Routed to partner (B2F)    Site outside direct IndiFrame coverage, or partner territory lead details to the partner and log C7 / ROUTE TO B2F in the CRM. Do not\n                                                                                                                      promise full IndiFrame service on partner leads.\n                                                                                                        Update the lead status as 'Won' in the CRM, initiate the order processing /\n    C4                Won Lead                       Payment Done, Manufacturing started                  manufacturing handover, and share the confirmation details with the\n                                                                                                                                        customer.\n                                                                                                        Record the specific reason for loss in the CRM, update lead status to 'Lost',\n    C6                Lost Lead                           Lost Due To Specific Reasons\n                                                                                                         and schedule a long-term nurturing or feedback follow-up if applicable.\n\n\n\n\nIf Customer Is Not Familiar with the Brand\n\nAgent: Sir/Ma'am, just to give you a quick idea about Indi Frame, we provide different types of windows\n\nand doors based on customer requirements, design preferences, and project needs. Our team can also\n\nguide you on which solution/type opt would be most suitable for your project.\n\nWhat Is UPVC?\n\nAgent: UPVC stands for Unplasticized Polyvinyl Chloride. It is a strong, durable, and low-maintenance\n\nmaterial commonly used for manufacturing windows and doors. It can provide good insulation and may\n\nhelp reduce outside noise and heat, depending on the overall window or door configuration.\n\nQuick Explanation\n\nAgent: Basically, Sir/Ma'am, Indi Frame provides uPVC and aluminum windows and doors in different\n\ndesigns and configurations such as sliding, casement, fixed, tilt & turn, and slide & fold. You don't need to\n\nworry about the technical details. Our team will understand your requirements and suggest the most\n\nsuitable option for your project.\n\nMANDATORY RENOVATION RULE – EXISTING WINDOWS & DOORS\n\n\nWhenever the customer says the project is a renovation, the agent MUST follow this sequence:\n\n   1. Confirm the existing windows and doors: Ask whether the customer will remove/uninstall the\n         existing windows and doors before IndiFrame work starts.\n<PARSED TEXT FOR PAGE: 3 / 16>\n   2. Make the requirement clear: Explain in simple words that the existing windows and doors must be\n      removed by the customer/their team before IndiFrame can start its work.\n   3. Confirm acceptance: Ask the customer if this arrangement is okay.\n   4. If the customer agrees: Ask for the expected date and time when the existing windows and\n      doors will be removed / the site will be ready for installation.\n   5. Ask for follow-up timing: Confirm a convenient date and time for IndiFrame to follow up and\n      coordinate the next step.\n   6. Do not confirm installation before the existing windows and doors are removed.\n\nApproved Customer Conversation:\n\nAgent: Since this is a renovation project, I’d like to confirm one important point. The existing windows and\ndoors will need to be removed before our work starts. Will you be able to get the existing windows and\ndoors removed before we begin?\n\nCustomer: Yes\n\n\nAgent: Great. Approximately when do you expect the existing windows and doors to be removed and the\nsite to be ready for our installation work?\n\nCustomer: [Date / Time] {After This have To Collect the Details as Per Script}\n\nAgent: Thank you. And what would be a convenient date and time for our team to follow up with you and\ncoordinate the next steps?\n\n\nIf Customer: [Follow-up Date / Time]\n\nAgent: Perfect. I’ve noted the site-readiness date and your preferred follow-up time. We will connect with\nyou accordingly.\n1 If the customer has NOT agreed to remove the existing windows and doors:\n\nAgent: No problem at all. However, please note that our team does not provide uninstalling services. We\ncan only start our installation work after the existing windows and doors have been completely removed\nby your team. May I please get your final confirmation that you understand and can arrange the\nUninstallation?\n\nCustomer: Must Decide\n\n\nAgent: Understood ___ Sir, May I Know what a convenient date and time for our team would be to follow\nup with you and coordinate the next steps?\n\nIf Customer: [Follow-up Date / Time]\n\nAgent: Perfect. I’ve noted the site-readiness date and your preferred follow-up time. We will connect with\nyou accordingly.\n\n\n\nCustomer: No\n\nAgent: Understood. Whenever you have completed removing the existing windows and doors and your\nsite is ready, you can call us back or reach us through the contact number (9959083498) mentioned on our\nwebsite. We’ll be happy to take the next steps with you!\n\n\n\nABUSIVE / INAPPROPRIATE LANGUAGE\n\n1st Attempt:\n\n\"I would request you to kindly use professional language.\"\n\n2nd Attempt:\n\n\n\"I would request you to kindly use professional language.\"\n\nClosing:\n\n\"As there is no positive response from your side, your call is being disconnected. Thank you for\nconsidering IndiFrame. We look forward to assisting you whenever you are ready. Have a wonderful day\nahead.\n\n2. BLANK CALL / NO RESPONSE (UNRESPONSIVE CUSTOMER)\n\n1st Attempt:\n\n\"Good morning, this is [Agent Name], calling from IndiFrame Windows and Doors,\n\n2nd Attempt:\n\n\" Good morning, this is [Agent Name], calling from IndiFrame Windows and Doors, please respond if you\nare on the call.\"\n\nClosing (If no response):\n<PARSED TEXT FOR PAGE: 4 / 16>\n\"As there is no response, the call is being disconnected. Thank you for considering IndiFrame. We look\nforward to assisting you whenever you are ready. Have a wonderful day ahead.\n\nCUSTOMER PUT ON HOLD (EXTENDED HOLD / UNATTENDED)]\n\n\n\n\n1st Attempt:\n\n\"As customer putted the call on hold, I have to disconnect the call forcefully.\"\n\n2nd Attempt:\n\n\"As the customer put the call on hold, I have to disconnect the call forcefully. Please respond if you are on\nthe call.\n\nClosing:\n\n\"As there is no response from your side, your call is being disconnected. Thank you for considering\nIndiFrame. We look forward to assisting you whenever you are ready. Have a wonderful day ahead.\n\n\n\nCustomer Does Not Answer / Call Is Forwarded to Voicemail\n\nAgent:\n“Hello, this is Mahesh calling from IndiFrame Windows and Doors regarding your enquiry. Please call us\nback at your convenience. Thank you.”\n\n\n\n4. Scenario A – Digital Ad Lead\n\nContext: Fresh enquiries from Meta, Google, Website, WhatsApp, or another digital channel.\n\nA1. Opening & Permission\n\nAgent:\n“Good evening, Sir, I am calling from IndiFrame, a premium brand in high-quality uPVC and Aluminum\nproducts/windows and doors. We received your enquiry regarding Windows & Doors on\n[Facebook/Instagram/WhatsApp/Website. Is this a good time for a quick Conversation?”\n\n\n\n\nA2. Core Requirement & Project Type\n\nAgent: Are you looking for windows or doors for your property?\n\nAgent: Is this for a new construction or renovation?\n\nAgent: Is this project for your residential home or commercial property?\n\nAgent: Which specific city and area/locality is your construction site located in?\n\n\n\n\nA3. Quantity, Material & Style\n\nAgent: How many windows and doors do you need? A rough count is completely fine for now.\n\n\n\nAgent: Do you have any type of windows and doors in your mind, such as sliding, casement, fixed, tilt &\nturn, or slide & fold?\n\n\n\nA4. Construction Stage, Readiness & Timeline..\n\nAgent: What stage is the site currently in — foundation, brickwork, plastering, or finishing?\n\nAgent: Approximately when are you planning to finalize or install the windows and doors?\n\nAgent: As a planning point, installation is best done after the granite or marble sill work is completed. Has\nthat work been completed at the site yet?\n\nIf Customer Wants Installation Before Granite/Marble Sill Work.\n\nCustomer: “I want the windows installed after plastering, before the granite/marble work.”\n\nAgent:\n“Sure, I’ll note it. Our sales team will check the site condition and confirm the suitable installation stage\nwith you.”\n\n\n\n\nA5. Decision Maker\n\nAgent: Will you be making the final purchase decision, or will an architect, builder, contractor, designer,\nor family member also be involved?\n<PARSED TEXT FOR PAGE: 5 / 16>\nIf others are involved:\n\nAgent:\n“If they are involved, it would be helpful if they could be part of the consultation so we can understand\neveryone’s requirements.”\n\n\n\n\nA6. Customer Questions / VOC\nAfter the qualification questions, the customer may have questions before deciding on the next step.\n\nCustomer: “Why should I buy from IndiFrame?”\n\nAgent:\n“IndiFrame is a pan-India brand, headquartered in Hyderabad. We provide uPVC and Aluminum\nwindows and doors, supported by a professional measurement team, well-trained installation team and\ndedicated after-sales service team. We follow an end-to-end process from measurement and\nmanufacturing to installation and after-sales support.”\n\n\n\n\nCustomer: “What are the benefits of using uPVC?”\n\nAgent:\n“uPVC is one of the window and door material options we provide. If you are considering uPVC, our team\ncan understand your project requirements and guide you on the suitable product and configuration based\non your application.”\n\nImportant: The agent should not add technical benefits that are not covered in the approved IndiFrame\nproduct material. Specific technical claims should be handled by the relevant sales/technical team.\n\n\n\n\nCustomer: “Why is your price high?”\n\nAgent:\n“I understand your concern regarding the price. The final price depends on the product, size,\nconfiguration, quantity, hardware, and other project requirements. Our team can understand your exact\nrequirement and explain the pricing accordingly.”\n\nAgent should not:\n\n      Promise a discount.\n      Compare pricing with competitors without approved information.\n      Give an unsupported final quotation.\n      Commit to a special price.\n\n\n\n\nCustomer: “Your competitor is offering it for less. Why should I choose IndiFrame?”\n\nAgent:\n“I understand. Pricing can vary depending on the product configuration, size, hardware and overall\nproject requirements. Our Sales Team can understand what you are comparing and explain the relevant\nIndiFrame offering and pricing for your project.”\n\n\n\n\nCustomer: “What makes IndiFrame different?”\n\nAgent:\n“We focus on an end-to-end process, including professional measurement, manufacturing, installation\nand after-sales service. We also use high-quality European machinery for manufacturing and have\ndedicated teams supporting the customer throughout the process.”\n\n\n\n\nCustomer: “Do you provide installation?”\n\nAgent:\n“Yes. We have a well-trained installation team, and our team will coordinate the installation based on the\nsite condition and the suitable installation stage.”\n\n\n\n\nCustomer: “Do you provide after-sales service?”\n\nAgent:\n“Yes. We have a dedicated service team for after-sales support.”\n\n\n\n\nCustomer: “Where are you located?”\n\nAgent:\n“IndiFrame is a pan-India brand, headquartered in Hyderabad. We are currently providing our services\n<PARSED TEXT FOR PAGE: 6 / 16>\nacross Andhra Pradesh, Maharashtra, and Telangana. We also have Experience Centers in Hyderabad and\nMumbai.”\n\nIf required:\n“Our team can guide, you regarding the Experience Centre most convenient for you.”\n\n\n\n\nCustomer: “Can I see your products before deciding?”\n\nAgent:\n“Certainly. You can visit our Experience Centre and explore the available product options and discuss\nyour project requirements with our team.”\n\n\n\n\nCustomer: “Can I visit your factory?”\n\nAgent:\n“Certainly. A factory visit can also be coordinated. Our team can guide you regarding the visit and help\nyou understand more about our manufacturing process and product range.”\n\n\n\n\nCustomer: “Can you give me the price now?”\n\nAgent:\n“We can understand your requirements and arrange for our Sales Team to discuss the pricing with you.\nThe final pricing depends on the specific requirements of your project.”\n\n\n\n\nCustomer: “Can you give me a discount?”\n\nAgent:\n“I understand your concern. Our Sales Team can discuss the applicable pricing for your specific\nrequirement.”\n\n\n\n\nCustomer: “How long will installation take?”\n\nAgent:\n“The installation timeline depends on the project requirements and site readiness. Our Sales Team will\nassess the requirement and coordinate the next steps with you.”\n\n\n\n\nA7. Closing – Based on Customer VOC\nAgent:\n“Thank you, Customer Name. That gives me a clear understanding of your requirements. Just to confirm,\nyou are looking for [Quantity & Type] windows and [Quantity & Type] doors for your\n[Residential/Commercial] project in [Location].\n\nBefore I proceed, may I know what would be convenient for you as the next step? Would you like to\ndiscuss your requirement with our Sales Team, arrange a Site Consultation, visit our Experience Centre, or\nwould you prefer a callback at a convenient date and time?”\n\nIf Customer agrees to proceed:\n\nAgent:\n“Certainly, Customer Name”. I’ll note your preferred next step as [Customer’s Requirement]. Our team\nwill coordinate with you regarding [Date/Time, if applicable] and take the discussion forward.”\n\nIf Customer wants some time / a later call:\n\nAgent:\n“Sure, Customer Name”. What date and time would be convenient for us to reach out to you?”\n\nAgent:\n“Perfect. I’ve noted [Date] at [Time]. Our team will contact you as discussed.”\n\nIf Customer is not interested / says No:\n\nAgent:\n“Certainly, Customer Name”. I understand. May I know if there is any reason for your decision, so I can\nnote your feedback correctly?”\n\nIf Customer shares the reason:\n\nAgent:\n“Understood. I’ve noted your feedback. Thank you for sharing that with us.”\n\nIf Customer does not want to share the reason:\n\nAgent:\n“I understand. Thank you for your time.”\n<PARSED TEXT FOR PAGE: 7 / 16>\nFinal Closing:\n\nAgent:\n“Thank you for considering IndiFrame. We look forward to assisting you whenever you are ready. Have a\nwonderful day ahead.”\n\n\n\n\n5. Scenario B – Field Spotted Lead\nContext: Lead collected through field sales, an active construction site, a site visit, or walk-by interaction.\n\nB1. Opening & Permission\nAgent:\nGood morning. I am calling on behalf of Indiframe Windows and Doors, a premium brand specializing in high-\nquality UPVC and Aluminum Product/Windows and Doors. Am I speaking with Mr./Ms. [Customer Name]? Our field\nofficer Mr./Ms. [Name] recently noted your construction work at [Location]. Since your site is under construction, is\nthis a good time to ask a few questions to understand your requirements and guide you properly?\n\n\n\nB2. Requirement & Existing Field Information\n\n  Collecting info when spotter details aren’t available :\n\n  Agent: Are you currently looking for windows or doors for this project, and could you please share the rough\n\n  quantity & type you need?\n\n  Agent: Are you considering uPVC, aluminum, or would you like our technical team to guide you? N/A\n\n  Agent: Do you have specific styles in mind, such as sliding, casement, fixed, tilt & turn, or slide & fold?\n\n  Confirmation of collective information :\n\n  Agent: As Per Our Notes It’s mentioned [15 Sliding Doors and 15 Sliding windows] and interest in [Casement/Turn\n\n  & Tilt or Combination windows]. Is that still correct?\n\n  Agent: Just to confirm, the project is located at [ Malak pet], is it correct?\n\n\n\n\nB3. Site Stage & Decision Maker\n\nCollecting info when spotter details aren’t available:\n\nAgent: What stage is the site currently in—foundation, brickwork, plastering, or finishing? -\n\nAgent: When do you expect the project to reach the windows and doors installation stage?\n\nAgent: As a planning point, installation is best done after granite or marble sill work is completed. Has that work\nbeen completed yet? N|A\n\nAgent: Will you be making the final decision, or will an architect, builder, contractor, designer, or family member\nalso be involved?\n\nConfirmation of collective information:\n\nAgent: Just to confirm, the site is currently at [Site Stage], and you are Making the Final decision? Or you will be\ncoordinating with [Stakeholder Type, e.g., your architect/family] for the final decision, is it correct?\n\n\nEnd-to-End Value Proposition\nAgent: \"Based on your Project, how would you like to proceed? Would you prefer a [Sales Team Callback / Site\nConsultation / Experience Centre Visit / Factory Visit / Partner Follow-Up?\"\n\nB4. Closing – Site Consultation\nCustomer: I would like a site consultation.\n\nAgent: Sure, Customer Name. Thank you for sharing your requirement. At IndiFrame, we provide free site\nconsultation, free professional measurements, custom-made manufacturing in our own factory, trained installation,\nand reliable after-sales support.\n\nAgent: Just to confirm again, you are looking for [Quantity & Type] windows and [Quantity & Type] doors for your\n[Residential/Commercial] project at [Location], and you would like to connect with our        sales team to coordinate\nthe site consultation and discuss the next steps with you.\n\nAgent: What would be a convenient date and time for our sales team to contact you about the site consultation?\n\nCustomer: [Date & Time]\n\nAgent: Perfect, [Customer Name]. I’ve noted the follow-up for [Date] at [Time]. Our sales team will connect with you\non that date and at that time to arrange the site consultation and assist you with the next steps.\n\nAgent: Thank you for considering IndiFrame. We look forward to assisting you with your project. Have a wonderful\nday ahead.\n\nB5. Closing – Sales Callback\n<PARSED TEXT FOR PAGE: 8 / 16>\nIf Customer Wants an Immediate Sales Callback\nCustomer: I would like someone from sales to call me.\n\nAgent: Sure, Customer Name. Thank you for sharing your requirement. At IndiFrame, we custom-make our products\nin our own factory, use our own trained installation team, and provide reliable after-sales service.\n\nAgent: Just to confirm again, you are looking for [Quantity & Type] windows and [Quantity & Type] doors for your\n[Residential/Commercial] project in [Location], [Customer Name] & you would like to discuss [Requirement/Concern]\nwith our sales team.\n\n\nIf Customer Didn’t Said for Immediate Call Back\n\n\nAgent: Sir, would you like to discuss [Requirement/Concern] with our sales team?\n\nCustomer: Yes, [Immediate].\n\nAgent: Sure, Sir/Ma’am. You can expect a call from our sales team within the next one hour. Thank you for\nconsidering IndiFrame. We look forward to assisting you with your project. Have a wonderful day ahead.\n\n\n\n\nIf Customer Wants the Sales Team to Call at a Specific Date & Time\nCustomer: Can you call me later?\n\nAgent: Sure, Customer Name. I can easily arrange a callback for you. What date and Time Is Coinvent to reach out?\n\nCustomer: [Date & Time]\n\nAgent: Perfect, [Customer Name]. Just to confirm again, you are looking for [Quantity & Type] windows and\n[Quantity & Type] doors for your [Residential/Commercial] project in [Location], and you would like our sales team\nto contact you about [Requirement/Concern] on [Date] at [Time].\n\nAgent: I’ve noted the details as discussed, and our sales team will connect with you on that date and at that time to\nassist you with the next steps.\n\nAgent: \"It was a pleasure speaking with you. Thank you for trusting IndiFrame For your project—have a great day!\"\n\n\n6. Scenario C – Expo / Event Lead\n\nContext: Customer visits an IndiFrame display, exhibition, or public event.\n\n\nC1. Opening & Permission\n\nAgent:\nGood morning. I am calling on behalf of Indiframe Windows and Doors, a premium brand specializing in high-\nquality UPVC and Aluminum Product/Windows and Doors. Am I speaking with Mr./Ms. [Customer Name]? We noted\nthat you visited our display at [Event Name] held on [Event Date] at [Event Location]. Is this a good time for a quick\nconversation?\n\nAgent: Great. Since you explored our products at the event, I wanted to understand your window and door\nrequirements so we can assist you properly. May I ask you a few quick questions?\n\n\n\n\nC2. Requirement & Existing Event Information\n\nAgent:\nAre you currently looking for windows, doors, or both for your project?\n\nAgent: Our event notes mention [Quantity] units and interest in [Type]. Is that still correct?\n\nAgent:\nJust to confirm, the project is located at [Location], correct?\n\nAgent:\nAre you considering uPVC, aluminum, or would you like our technical team to guide you?\n\nAgent:\nDo you have specific styles in mind, such as sliding, casement, fixed, tilt & turn, or slide & fold?\n\nAgent:\nWhat is the main priority for your project — for example, appearance, ventilation, natural light, sound reduction, or\nease of operation safety sound insulation, heat reduction, and privacy?\n\n\n\n\nC3. Project Stage & Decision Maker\n\nAgent:\nIs this for a new construction, an upcoming renovation?\n\nAgent:\nWhat stage is the project currently in — foundation, brickwork, plastering, or finishing?\n<PARSED TEXT FOR PAGE: 9 / 16>\nAgent:\nHave internal and external plastering been completed around the window openings?\n\nAgent:\nWhen do you expect the project to reach the window and door installation stage?\n\nAgent:\nAs a planning point, installation is best done after granite or marble sill work is completed. Has that work been\ncompleted yet?\n\nAgent:\nWill you be making the final decision, or will an architect, builder, contractor, designer, or family member also be\ninvolved?\n\n\nEnd-to-End Value Proposition\nAgent: \"Based on your Project, how would you like to proceed? Would you prefer a [Sales Team Callback / Site\nConsultation / Experience Centre Visit / Factory Visit / Partner Follow-Up?\"\n\n\nC4. Closing – Site Consultation\n\nCustomer: I would like a site consultation.\n\nAgent: Sure, Customer Name. Thank you for sharing your requirement. At IndiFrame, we provide free site\nconsultation, free professional measurements, custom-made manufacturing in our own factory, trained installation,\nand reliable after-sales support.\n\nAgent: Just to confirm again, you are looking for [Quantity & Type] windows and [Quantity & Type] doors for your\n[Residential/Commercial] project at [Location], and you would like our sales team to arrange the site consultation\nand discuss the next steps with you.\n\nAgent: What would be a convenient date and time for our sales team to contact you about the site consultation?\n\nCustomer: [Date & Time]\n\nAgent: Perfect, [Customer Name]. I’ve noted the follow-up for [Date] at [Time]. Our sales team will connect with you\non that date and at that time to arrange the site consultation and assist you with the next steps.\n\nAgent: \"We sincerely thank you for considering IndiFrame. Please let us know if you need anything else as you get\nstarted, Have a wonderful day ahead.\n\n\nC5. Closing – Sales Callback\n\nIf Customer Wants an Immediate Sales Callback\n\nCustomer: I would like someone from sales to call me.\n\nAgent: Sure, Customer Name. Thank you for sharing your requirement. At IndiFrame, we custom-make our\nproducts in our own factory, use our own trained installation team, and provide reliable after-sales service.\n\nAgent: Just to confirm again, you are looking for [Quantity & Type] windows and [Quantity & Type] doors for your\n[Residential/Commercial] project in [Location], and you would like to discuss [Requirement/Concern] with our sales\nteam.\n\nAgent: You can expect a call from our sales team within the next one hour. They will assist you with your\nrequirements and guide you through the next steps.\n\nAgent: \"It was a pleasure speaking with you. Thank you for trusting IndiFrame with your project—have a great\nday!\"\n\n\nIf Customer Wants the Sales Team to Call at a Specific Date & Time\n\nCustomer: Can you call me later?\n\nAgent: Sure, Customer Name. I can easily arrange a callback for you. What date and time are convenient to reach\nout?\n\nCustomer: [Date & Time]\n\nAgent: Perfect, [Customer Name]. Just to reconfirm, you are looking for [Quantity & Type] windows and [Quantity\n& Type] doors for your [Residential/Commercial] project in [Location], and you would like our sales team to\ncontact you regarding [Requirement/Concern] on [Date] at [Time].\n\nAgent: I’ve noted the details accordingly, and our sales team will connect with you on that date and at that time to\nassist you with the next steps.\n\nAgent: \"It was a pleasure speaking with you. Thank you for trusting IndiFrame with your project—have a great\nday!\"\n\n\nC6. Closing – Experience Centre Visit\n\nCustomer: I would like to visit the Experience Centre.\n\nAgent: Wonderful, Customer Name. Just to reconfirm, you are looking for [Quantity & Type] windows and [Quantity\n& Type] doors for your [Residential/Commercial] project in [Location]. You have chosen to visit our [Kukatpally /\nJubilee Hills / Malad West] Experience Centre.\n\nAgent: What would be a convenient date and time for you to visit the Experience Centre?\n<PARSED TEXT FOR PAGE: 10 / 16>\nCustomer: [Date & Time]\n\nAgent: Perfect, [Customer Name]. I’ve noted your preferred visit for [Date] at [Time]. Our team will coordinate with\nyou and assist you during your visit.\n\nAgent: You’ll have an opportunity to explore our product options and discuss your project requirements with our\nteam. Thank you for showing your interest in IndiFrame. We look forward to assisting you with your project. Have a\nwonderful day ahead.\n\n\n\nC7. Closing – Medchal Factory Visit\n\nCustomer: I would like to visit the factory.\n\n\nAgent: Excellent, [Customer Name]. Just to reconfirm, you are looking for [Quantity & Type] windows and [Quantity\n& Type] doors for your [Residential/Commercial] project in [Location]. You have chosen to visit our Medchal factory.\n\nAgent: What would be a convenient date and time for you to visit the Medchal factory?\n\nCustomer: [Factory Visit Date & Time]\n\nAgent: Perfect, [Customer Name]. I’ll note your preferred factory visit for [Date] at [Time], and our team will\ncoordinate the visit with you.\n\nAgent: During the visit, you can understand more about our manufacturing process and product range. \"It was a\npleasure speaking with you. Thank you for trusting IndiFrame with your project—have a great day!\"\n\n7. Scenario D – Stage Follow-Up / Warm Lead / Construction Delay\n\n  Context: Existing lead where the customer was previously waiting for construction progress, budget, timing, or a\n\n  decision.\n\n\nOpening & Permission\nAgent: Good morning. I am calling on behalf of Indiframe Windows and Doors, a premium brand specializing in\nhigh-quality UPVC and Aluminum Product/Windows and Doors. We spoke about [Number of days/weeks] ago about\nyour window and door requirements for [Project/Location]. I wanted to quickly check in and understand how your\nproject is moving along. Is this a good time?\n\nAgent: Thank you. Have there been any recent updates on the construction or renovation?\n\nD2. Confirm Again Previous Requirement\nAgent: According to our notes from our last conversation, you were looking at [Quantity] units of [Type]. Have there\nbeen any changes to the requirement or quantity?\n\nAgent: Have you had a chance to review the details or quotation from our side, or is there anything specific you are\nevaluating right now?\n\nD3. Construction Delay / Stage Advice\nAgent: No problem at all. Construction timelines can change. Just as a helpful planning point, we recommend\nscheduling window and door installation after the granite or marble sill work is completed. What stage are your\nwalls and sills at now, and when do you expect to reach that point?\n\nD4. Budget / Price Discussion\nAgent: I understand, [Customer Name]. Budget management is an important part of any project. Are you comparing\nour quotation with another branded provider or a local vendor? Understanding what you are evaluating will help\nour team guide you properly.\n\nAgent: IndiFrame focuses on complete value through professional consultation, measurements, custom-made\nmanufacturing, trained installation, and after-sales support.\n\n\nEnd-to-End Value Proposition\nAgent: \"Based on your Project, how would you like to proceed? Would you prefer a [Sales Team Callback / Site\nConsultation / Experience Centre Visit / Factory Visit / Partner Follow-Up?\"\n\nD5. Closing – Future Follow-Up\nAgent: Thank you, Customer Name. That gives me a clear picture of your current requirements. Just to confirm\nagain, you are looking for [Quantity & Type] windows and [Quantity & Type] doors for your\n[Residential/Commercial] project in [Location], and you would like our [Sales/Concerned] Team to discuss\n[Concern/Requirement].\n\nAgent: Our team will follow up with you on [Date] at [Time]. I’ve noted this as discussed, and we’ll keep you updated\non the next steps.\n\nAgent: Thank you for your time today. We look forward to assisting you when you are ready.\n\nD6. Closing – Immediate Site Consultation\nAgent: Thank you, Customer Name. Just to confirm again, you are looking for [Quantity & Type] windows and\n[Quantity & Type] doors at [Location]. Our sales team will follow up with you on [Date] at [Time] to arrange the site\nconsultation and next steps. Thank you for considering IndiFrame. We look forward to welcoming you and assisting\nyou with your project. Have a good day.\n<PARSED TEXT FOR PAGE: 11 / 16>\n  8. Scenario E – Location Outside Direct Service Area/Green Fortune Fabricator\n\n  Partner/Unserviceable location\n\nContext: The project site falls outside Indi Frame's direct installation coverage and must be routed to an authorized\nGreen Fortune partner.\n\nE1. Opening & Permission\nAgent: Good morning. I am calling on behalf of Indiframe Windows and Doors, a premium brand specializing in\nhigh-quality UPVC and Aluminum Product/Windows and Doors, about your enquiry. Is this a good time for a quick\nconversation?\n\n\nMay I ask you a few quick questions?\n\nE2. Requirement & Existing Enquiry Information\n\nAgent: Are you currently looking for windows, doors, or both for this project?\n\nAgent: Our enquiry details mention [Quantity] units and interest in [Casement, Sliding Tilt and Turn and fixed Slide\nand fold]. Is that still correct?\n\nAgent: Just to confirm, the project is located at [Customer Location], correct?\n\nAgent: Are you considering uPVC, aluminum, or would you like the technical team to guide you? N/A\n\nAgent: Do you have specific styles in mind, such as sliding, casement, fixed, tilt & turn, or slide & fold? N/A\n\n\nAgent: Great. I understand your project is located at [Customer Location], Since our direct installation teams operate\nselectively in our main service locations, I wanted to understand your project requirements and connect you with\nthe appropriate green fortune Fabricator partner.\n\n\n\nAgent: I understand, [Customer Name]. Budget/Quality is an important part of any construction project. When\ncomparing options, it is useful to consider the overall value, including material quality. Green's fortune provides a\ncomplete process, so the customer has one team arranged throughout the project.\n\nE3. Site Stage & Decision Maker\nAgent: Is this for a new construction or renovation? N\n\nAgent: What stage is the project currently in — foundation, brickwork, plastering, or finishing?\n\nAgent: When do you expect the project to reach the window and door installation stage?\n\nAgent: As a planning point, installation is best done after granite or marble sill work is completed. Has that work\nbeen completed yet?\n\nAgent: Will you be making the final decision/decision, or will an architect, builder, contractor, designer, or family\nmember also be involved?\n\n\n\n\nEnd-to-End Value Proposition\nAgent: \"Based on your Project, how would you like to proceed? Would you prefer a [Sales Team Callback /Partner"}
